WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.826
Picture your first week. A message arrives. "Our retailer says they never got our invoices from last Tuesday. Can you look?"

00:00:07.826 --> 00:00:16.776
To answer well, you need four things. Know the business, read the platform, find whose problem it is, and explain it in two clear sentences.

00:00:16.776 --> 00:00:22.751
That is the job. Think of an interpreter at a meeting, where two companies speak different languages.

00:00:22.751 --> 00:00:30.426
Our client's system speaks NetSuite. The retailer speaks E D I, their own way. We make sure every message keeps its meaning.

00:00:30.426 --> 00:00:34.626
We also build the interpreting booth, test it, and keep it running.

00:00:34.626 --> 00:00:45.452
Inbound, a retailer sends an eight fifty purchase order. Orderful checks it and turns it into Jason, a modern data format. NetSuite creates a sales order.

00:00:45.452 --> 00:00:56.152
Outbound, the client ships in NetSuite. That creates an eight fifty six ship notice, and later an eight ten invoice. Orderful turns them into the partner's exact format.

00:00:56.152 --> 00:01:02.252
Every project has four groups of people. The client, the trading partner, Orderful, and us.

00:01:02.252 --> 00:01:08.952
The client owns their E R P and their data. They need clear asks and honest status, without jargon.

00:01:08.952 --> 00:01:16.202
The trading partner owns their spec and their go-live approval. They need correct documents and one clear contact.

00:01:16.202 --> 00:01:25.102
Orderful owns the platform, and needs us to lead and arrive with solutions. To clients and partners, we are part of the Orderful team.

00:01:25.102 --> 00:01:31.927
The life of a project. It starts with kickoff and scope. Which partners, which documents, and who decides.

00:01:31.927 --> 00:01:38.527
Then partner outreach, then build and map, so the client's data fills every field the partner needs.

00:01:38.527 --> 00:01:44.452
Then we test on the test stream, a safe lane that never reaches the partner's real systems.

00:01:44.452 --> 00:01:50.202
Then go-live ready. Careful. Testing complete is a milestone. It does not mean live.

00:01:50.202 --> 00:01:57.428
Then we switch to live, and hypercare begins. We watch every real document daily. Finally, steady support.

00:01:57.428 --> 00:02:06.553
Most days, a partner rejects a document, a record was not created in the E R P, a new partner needs turning on, or something is stuck.

00:02:06.553 --> 00:02:12.503
A real lesson. Never tell a client something is fixed from memory. Check the platform first.

00:02:12.503 --> 00:02:18.228
If you are guessing, say so. "Likely cause, not verified yet" protects your credibility.

00:02:18.228 --> 00:02:23.778
And every open item needs one owner and a date. "In progress" is not a status.

00:02:23.778 --> 00:02:31.728
You are the interpreter, the builder, and the guardian. Scope it, build it, test it safely, switch it on, then watch it closely.

00:02:31.728 --> 00:02:36.228
Next, we follow one order all the way from purchase order to cash.

